{"findings":[{"topic":"Express 4 TypeScript CRUD with In-Memory Store","summary":"Standard pattern: maintain a module-level array + auto-increment ID counter. Each CRUD function (getAll, getById, create, update, delete) is a pure function exported from a separate store module. Routes use Router(), destructure typed Request/Response params, return 404 for missing resources, 400 for invalid input, 204 (no body) for DELETE, 201 for POST. Global error middleware catches unhandled throws.","source":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/build-a-rest-api-with-express-js-and-typescript/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"// server/store.ts
const users: User[] = [];
let nextId = 1;
export const createUser = (data: Omit<User, 'id'>): User => {
  const user = { id: nextId++, ...data };
  users.push(user);
  return user;
};

// server/routes/users.ts
router.post('/', (req, res) => {
  const { name, email } = req.body;
  if (!name || !email) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'name and email required' });
  res.status(201).json(createUser({ name, email, avatarUrl: req.body.avatarUrl ?? null }));
});
router.delete('/:id', (req, res) => {
  if (!deleteUser(Number(req.params.id))) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
  res.status(204).send();
});","codeExample2":"// Global error middleware (must be last, 4-arg signature)
app.use((err: Error, _req: Request, res: Response, _next: NextFunction) => {
  console.error(err.stack);
  res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
});"},{"topic":"React 18 Custom Hook: useFetch with loading/error/refetch","summary":"Pattern: generic useFetch<T>(url, refreshKey) hook using useState + useEffect. Cleanup via cancelled flag prevents state updates after unmount (critical for React 18 StrictMode double-invoke). Refetch is triggered by incrementing a refreshKey counter passed as a dep. Error set from res.ok check before parsing JSON.","source":"https://www.robinwieruch.de/react-hooks-fetch-data/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"// src/hooks/useUsers.ts
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import type { User } from '../types/user';

export function useUsers() {
  const [users, setUsers] = useState<User[]>([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);
  const [refreshKey, setRefreshKey] = useState(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    let cancelled = false;
    setLoading(true);
    setError(null);
    fetch('/api/users')
      .then(res => { if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`); return res.json() as Promise<User[]>; })
      .then(data => { if (!cancelled) { setUsers(data); setLoading(false); } })
      .catch(err => { if (!cancelled) { setError(err.message); setLoading(false); } });
    return () => { cancelled = true; };
  }, [refreshKey]);

  const refresh = () => setRefreshKey(k => k + 1);
  return { users, loading, error, refresh };
}"},{"topic":"React 18 Form State Pattern (no external library)","summary":"Single form state object with computed handleChange using [e.target.name]. Separate submitting + formError states. handleSubmit: preventDefault, set submitting=true, fetch POST/PUT, throw on !res.ok, call onSuccess callback, catch sets formError, finally clears submitting. Inline validation before fetch call.","source":"https://www.robinwieruch.de/react-hooks-fetch-data/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"// src/components/UserForm.tsx
type Props = { onSuccess: () => void; initial?: Partial<User>; userId?: number };

export default function UserForm({ onSuccess, initial, userId }: Props) {
  const [form, setForm] = useState({ name: initial?.name ?? '', email: initial?.email ?? '', avatarUrl: initial?.avatarUrl ?? '' });
  const [submitting, setSubmitting] = useState(false);
  const [formError, setFormError] = useState<string | null>(null);

  const handleChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) =>
    setForm(prev => ({ ...prev, [e.target.name]: e.target.value }));

  const handleSubmit = async (e: React.FormEvent) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    if (!form.name.trim() || !form.email.trim()) { setFormError('Name and email are required'); return; }
    setSubmitting(true);
    setFormError(null);
    try {
      const url = userId ? `/api/users/${userId}` : '/api/users';
      const res = await fetch(url, { method: userId ? 'PUT' : 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify(form) });
      if (!res.ok) { const body = await res.json(); throw new Error(body.error ?? `HTTP ${res.status}`); }
      onSuccess();
    } catch (err) {
      setFormError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Unknown error');
    } finally { setSubmitting(false); }
  };
  return ( /* JSX form with Tailwind */ );
}"},{"topic":"Tailwind CSS patterns for loading/error/card UI","summary":"Loading spinner: animate-spin with border-t-transparent. Error banner: bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-500 text-red-700. Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow. Form input: w-full px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500. Avatar with fallback: object-cover w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-gray-200.","source":"https://www.robinwieruch.de/react-hooks-fetch-data/","relevance":"medium","codeExample":"// Loading
<div className="flex justify-center py-12">
  <div className="animate-spin w-8 h-8 border-4 border-blue-500 border-t-transparent rounded-full" />
</div>
// Error
<div className="bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-500 text-red-700 p-4 rounded-r-lg">{error}</div>
// Card
<div className="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow p-4 flex items-center gap-4">
  <img src={user.avatarUrl || undefined} className="w-12 h-12 rounded-full object-cover bg-gray-200" />
  <div><p className="font-semibold text-gray-900">{user.name}</p><p className="text-sm text-gray-500">{user.email}</p></div>
</div>
// Input
<input className="w-full px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 disabled:opacity-50" />"},{"topic":"Vite Dev Proxy for Express API","summary":"When Vite (port 5173) and Express (port 3001) run on different ports, fetch('/api/users') hits port 5173 and fails. Must add a proxy config to vite.config.ts so /api/* requests are forwarded to http://localhost:3001. This avoids CORS entirely in dev.","source":"local knowledge — standard Vite pattern","relevance":"high","codeExample":"// vite.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  server: {
    proxy: {
      '/api': {
        target: 'http://localhost:3001',
        changeOrigin: true,
      }
    }
  }
});"}],"recommendations":["CREATE src/types/user.ts first: interface User { id: number; name: string; email: string; avatarUrl: string | null; }. Export as named export. This is the single source of truth used by both hook and components.","CREATE server/store.ts as a separate module with in-memory array + nextId counter. Export pure functions: getAllUsers, getUserById, createUser, updateUser, deleteUser. Import User type from a shared or duplicated interface (server has its own tsconfig scope).","UPDATE server/index.ts: add express.json() middleware, mount user router at /api/users, add 4-argument global error handler as the LAST middleware. Routes: GET /, GET /:id, POST / (validate name+email), PUT /:id, DELETE /:id (204 no body).","ADD Vite proxy in vite.config.ts: server.proxy['/api'] → target http://localhost:3001. This is REQUIRED — without it, fetch('/api/users') from the React app on port 5173 will 404 against Vite, not Express.","CREATE src/services/userService.ts: typed async functions (getUsers, createUser, updateUser, deleteUser) that call fetch, check res.ok, parse JSON, and throw typed errors. Centralizes fetch logic so hooks stay clean.","CREATE src/hooks/useUsers.ts: uses useState + useEffect with cancelled cleanup flag. Returns { users, loading, error, refresh }. refresh() increments a refreshKey to re-trigger the effect. No external library needed.","CREATE src/components/UserForm.tsx: single form state object, handleChange using computed [e.target.name], separate submitting+formError states. Supports both create (no userId prop) and edit (userId + initial props) modes. Call onSuccess() on completion — parent decides whether to close modal or refresh list.","CREATE src/components/UserCard.tsx: display-only card with avatar (img with fallback background), name, email, Edit and Delete buttons. Delete triggers a confirmation (window.confirm) before calling deleteUser service. Accepts onEdit and onDelete callbacks.","CREATE src/components/UserList.tsx: calls useUsers hook, renders loading spinner / error banner / empty state / grid of UserCards. Manages edit modal state (selectedUser). Renders UserForm in an overlay/modal for create and edit.","UPDATE src/App.tsx: remove all boilerplate (counter, Vite logo, etc.), import and render UserList as the main content. Wrap in a simple layout div with Tailwind container/padding.","DIRECTORY STRUCTURE to create: src/types/, src/services/, src/hooks/, src/components/ — Vite/TypeScript will pick them up automatically, no config changes needed.","avatarUrl should be optional in the form (empty string → null on the server). Add a fallback UI in UserCard (div with user initials) when avatarUrl is null."],"warnings":["CORS ISSUE: Without the Vite proxy config, all fetch('/api/...') calls from localhost:5173 will fail with a 404 or CORS error. The proxy is the cleanest dev solution — do not add cors() middleware to Express as a workaround (it's unnecessary with the proxy).","TypeScript strict mode + noUnusedLocals: every imported type and variable must be used. The 4-arg error handler needs _req and _next prefixed with underscore or TypeScript will complain about unused parameters.","React 18 StrictMode double-invoke: components mount twice in dev. The cancelled flag in useEffect cleanup is not optional — without it, you'll see duplicate fetches setting state on unmounted components and React will warn.","Express body parsing: express.json() middleware MUST be added before routes in server/index.ts. Without it, req.body is undefined and all POST/PUT handlers break silently.","No test framework is configured. The implementation should work as-is, but type errors in server/ won't be caught by tsc (tsx runs without tsc). Run npx tsc --noEmit manually if type safety on the server matters.","avatarUrl: do not use <img src={null}> — React will render a broken image icon. Always guard: src={user.avatarUrl || undefined} or conditionally render the img element.","DELETE 204 response has no body — do not call res.json() on a 204 response. The frontend should check res.status === 204 and not call res.json(), or call res.ok and skip json parsing for deletes.","ID type: the in-memory store uses number IDs (auto-increment). Express route params are strings — always convert with Number(req.params.id). Consider validating isNaN() to return 400 for non-numeric IDs.","The project uses single quotes in server TS and double quotes in JSX attributes per conventions — maintain this. TSConfig strict mode will catch type errors but not style issues (no linter configured).","No persistence: the in-memory store resets every time the server restarts. This is acceptable for a demo but should be noted clearly if the user expects data to survive restarts."]}}

