{"findings":[{"topic":"Express 4 TypeScript CRUD with In-Memory Store","summary":"Standard pattern: maintain a module-level array + auto-increment ID counter. Each CRUD function (getAll, getById, create, update, delete) is a pure function exported from a separate store module. Routes use Router(), destructure typed Request/Response params, return 404 for missing resources, 400 for invalid input, 204 (no body) for DELETE, 201 for POST. Global error middleware catches unhandled throws.","source":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/build-a-rest-api-with-express-js-and-typescript/","relevance":"high","codeExample":"// server/store.ts
const users: User[] = [];
let nextId = 1;
export const createUser = (data: Omit<User, 'id'>): User => {
  const user = { id: nextId++, ...data };
  users.push(user);
  return user;
};

// server/routes/users.ts
router.post('/', (req, res) => {
  const { name, email } = req.body;
  if (!name || !email) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'name and email required' });
  res.status(201).json(createUser({ name, email, avatarUrl: req.body.avatarUrl ?? null }));
});
router.delete('/:id', (req, res) => {
